[Music]  I've seen solo a Star Wars story and I  have thoughts this is a spoiler free  review and it's gonna go a little all  over the place because to be totally  honest I have mixed feelings about the  movie I went in expecting this  completely familiar kind of nostalgic  feel kind of a summer flick but this  movie has an unexpectedly bold adventure  that reaches depths of the Star Wars  galaxy I never thought imaginable on the  big screen exploring young Han Solo to  me was a gutsy move this character has  never carried his own movie and you're  giving it to a brand-new young actor now  much like the other anthology Star Wars  movie rogue one solo is not about the  Jedi thus if the force or lightsabers it  doesn't have an opening crawl it's not  scored by John Williams and you have  three new actors portraying three  beloved characters we've known most of  if not our entire lives these aren't  necessarily negative criticisms but it's  worth noting why it might take a hot  minute to adjust to the fact that you  are watching a Star Wars movie it took  me about 30 minutes or so to feel like  solo it found its footing and that's  right around the time that Lando  Calrissian comes into play but once it  gets going it makes the jump to  Lightspeed and it does not slow down  there was a lot of talk a  behind-the-scenes drama legendary  screenwriter lawrence kasdan who wrote  The Empire Strikes Back Return of the  Jedi and the force awakens teamed up  with a son John Kasdan to penned the  flick and Ron Howard who was in George  Lucas pre Star Wars movie American  Graffiti by the way 1973 stepped into  direct late in the game after Phil Lord  and Christopher Miller departed over  creative differences and you might see  people saying that they picked this up  on screen but I I truly didn't notice  plus the combo of Howard and Kasim kind  of brings a sense sense of warmth to the  movie much like Han Solo himself this  movie isn't without flaws but none of  those flaws stem from Alden Ehrenreich  spur trail of the iconic smuggler I  never doubted this guy always loved him  but there were reports he had to have an  acting coach on set and fans were  panicking but know this dude has all the  roguish charm that makes up Han Solo  without doing a single impersonation of  Harrison Ford's rather impressive you  probably expected this one but Donnell  Glover's take on the suave Lando  Calrissian and his many capes is a  scene-stealer through and through in  fact some of the biggest laps for me in  a Star Wars movie to date came courtesy  of Lando and his overtly sassy Droid and  co-pilot l 3-3-7 played by Phoebe Waller  bridge she really goes there  now the newcomers all bring something to  the table but the heart of solo was  completely about Han and Chewie the  budding relationship we get to see these  two meet for the first time and lay down  the foundation of what brought them  together as co-pilots and BFFs and  you've got a tip your hat to Jonas to  otama and Alden Ehrenreich seamless  chemistry now Jonas kind of discreetly  snuck into the Star Wars franchise to  take on some more action intensive  scenes for Peter Mayhew  in the force awakens and has since kind  of quietly taken over the reins as  Chewbacca almost entirely and they're  finally starting to bring him to the  forefront and I just really enjoyed his  performance in this movie I think he's  so fantastic anyway as I mentioned Solo  goes some unexpected places for better  and for worse when you bring together a  young Han Chewie and Lando I expect  these well known kind of nostalgic feats  like the Kessel run  Chuy's life-debt han winning over the  Falcon from Lando and some of these  things happen some don't but the ones  they do tell are in very surprising ways  like you may assume tell things happened  and went down in your head Cannon and  it's not that way at all it brings  surprising new facets to these legendary  tales while throwing in brand new  concepts and characters and some big  surprises that tie in the Star Wars lore  as a whole together in a very daring way  I wasn't terribly worried about spoilers  ahead of solo but having seen it I urge  you to avoid them at all costs solo is  gonna challenge viewers to dive deeper  into the mythos of Star Wars and it will  be very interesting to see how these  gutsier moments are received among  general audiences and whether or not  diehard fans are on board with the  direction the possible saga could take I  found it a little bold for the big  screen but we'll see I'm still  processing we're gonna dive deeper into  spoilers after release there's so much  unpacking so much that I want to openly  talk about but we have to wait at the  end of the day though solo is a fun  movie you're gonna have a smile on your  face gonna have a really good time and  of course you can tweet me any  spoiler-free questions you have I'm  happy to answer them as long as they're  spoiler free you can see solo on May  25th  may the force be with you  [Applause]

